# Pokemon Crystal LIVE link trade + CLOCK CHECK, host side.  The session runs
# on real clocks (no gblink_rtc_seed; the host's clock reads 2011); after it
# the game boots from its battery save (gblink_resume = 2) and must reach
# the overworld without "The clock's time may be wrong".
# From here as gen2_live_host.ap:
# (the gen2_counter_host.ap end state, standing at the Cable Trade Center
# receptionist) -- no boot, no restart.  The host disconnects after the
# trade (the menu's Disconnect); both then play on.
hold UP 8
wait 20
# YES, wait for the friend, save, and walk in (map 20:2 TRADE_CENTER)
mash A 1 0xDCB6 0xFF 2 4000
evt in_trade_center
wait 120
# --- the internal-clock side sits at (3,4) facing right, the other at
# (6,4) facing left (TradeCenter.asm; hSerialConnectionStatus $FFCB = 2)
stepram UP 1 0xDCB7 0xFF 5 1000
ifram 1 0xFFCB 0xFF 2 3
stepram LEFT 1 0xDCB8 0xFF 3 1000
stepram UP 1 0xDCB7 0xFF 4 1000
hold RIGHT 8
ifram 1 0xFFCB 0xFF 1 3
stepram RIGHT 1 0xDCB8 0xFF 6 1000
stepram UP 1 0xDCB7 0xFF 4 1000
hold LEFT 8
wait 20
logbytes seat 2 0xDCB7
hold A 6
wait 800
# --- our first Pokemon (GROWLITHE "Jacob"): STATS/TRADE -> TRADE, confirm
hold A 6
wait 60
hold RIGHT 6
wait 30
hold A 6
wait 400
mash A 1 0xDCD8 0xFF 0xA0 4000
evt traded
# The games save by themselves once the trade animation ends (~90 s).
# Not waitsram: both use cartridge RAM as scratch for Pokemon pictures, so
# its CRC moves long before the save lands.  score_trade.py judges the save.
wait 5400
evt settled
logbytes party 7 0xDCD7
disconnect
# --- past the session's end (margin + any deferrals), into the reboot
wait 1400
evt rebooted
repeat 5
wait 120
press START
endrepeat
wait 200
hold A 8
wait 60
hold A 8
wait 180
evt booted
logbytes where 4 0xDCB5
waitramne 1 0xDCB5 0xFF 0 600
hold DOWN 20
wait 60
logbytes moved 4 0xDCB5
# the step landed: y 3 -> 4 (PC 2F, where the trade's save put us)
waitram 1 0xDCB7 0xFF 4 60
evt clock_ok
